"""The third shape: a member that designates its entry point ONLY in `exports`.

No `main` and no `module`, which is how a package published for a modern resolver
is written -- and how most of a monorepo's own packages are. A hub that reads
only `main` has nothing to walk from and is left with the member's root as the
only candidate; the default boundary mode puts the target here instead, so that
hub declares no target for the member and the name stops resolving.
"""

load("@rules_typescript//ts:defs.bzl", "ts_compile")

ts_compile(
    name = "src",
    srcs = ["index.ts"],
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
